# SQL's `left` as a join kind: DS0123 with a fix to `leftouter`.
mode: syntax
---- query
'orders.csv' | join kind = left 'customers.csv' on customerId
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..62
  PIPELINE@0..61
    LITERAL@0..12
      STRING@0..12 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
    PIPE@13..14 "|"
    WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
    JOIN_OP@15..61
      IDENT@15..19 "join"
      WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
      JOIN_KIND@20..31
        IDENT@20..24 "kind"
        WHITESPACE@24..25 " "
        EQ@25..26 "="
        WHITESPACE@26..27 " "
        IDENT@27..31 "left"
      WHITESPACE@31..32 " "
      LITERAL@32..47
        STRING@32..47 "'customers.csv'"
      WHITESPACE@47..48 " "
      IDENT@48..50 "on"
      WHITESPACE@50..51 " "
      NAME_REF@51..61
        IDENT@51..61 "customerId"
  WHITESPACE@61..62 "\n"

error[DS0123]: unknown join kind `left`
  --> query:1:28
  |
1 | 'orders.csv' | join kind = left 'customers.csv' on customerId
  |                            ^^^^ not a join kind
  |
  = help: write `kind = leftouter`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    'orders.csv' | join kind = leftouter 'customers.csv' on customerId
which parses without errors
